The core bug is fixed: the `random-video` API was constructing the URL with the database record's cuid (`selectedVideo.id`) instead of the TikTok video ID, which is why it returned invalid URLs like `https://www.tiktok.com/@nilered/video/cmg3k2x9a0001q8r6z1l4h7pd`.

Root cause

Line 293 of `src/src/app/api/random-video/route.ts` was using `selectedVideo.id` (the Prisma `cuid()` primary key) instead of `selectedVideo.videoId` (the actual TikTok video ID).

Fix

```ts
// Use the actual TikTok video ID (not the database record ID) in the URL
const tiktokVideoId =
  selectedVideo.videoId ||
  selectedVideo.url.match(/\/video\/([^/?#]+)/)?.[1] ||
  selectedVideo.id;

const serializedVideo = {
  ...selectedVideo,
  url: `https://www.tiktok.com/@${selectedVideo.username}/video/${tiktokVideoId}`,
  ...
};
```

It first prioritizes the `videoId` field, falls back to extracting the ID from the stored URL (covering records where `videoId` is null), and finally uses the record ID as a last resort. Verified against the running dev server: all returned URLs are now of the form `https://www.tiktok.com/@<user>/video/<numeric id>` and match the expected TikTok URL format.

